        "summary": "Cancellation can be missed while the command log is being opened. Timeout handling otherwise targets the owned process group and marks execution unsuccessful.",
        "coverage": "complete",
        "omissions": [],
        "findings": [
          {
            "title": "Recheck cancellation after asynchronous log setup",
            "consequence": "If the signal is aborted during log setup, the initial check has already passed and the abort listener is registered too late to receive the event. The command then starts and can finish with code 0 and cancelled=false, which requireSuccess accepts. Otherwise it continues until its timeout instead of terminating promptly on cancellation.",
            "owner": "review/process.mjs command",
            "severity": "medium",
            "evidence": [
              {
                "kind": "source",
                "path": "review/process.mjs",
                "side": "head",
                "line": 8,
                "checkId": "",
                "quote": "  if (signal?.aborted) return { code: null, cancelled: true, stdout: '', stderr: '', elapsedMs: 0 };"
              },
              {
                "kind": "source",
                "path": "review/process.mjs",
                "side": "head",
                "line": 12,
                "checkId": "",
                "quote": "    await mkdir(dirname(log), { recursive: true, mode: 0o700 });\n    file = await open(log, 'wx', 0o600);\n    await file.write(`${JSON.stringify({ argv, cwd, started: new Date(started).toISOString() })}\\n`);"
              },
              {
                "kind": "source",
                "path": "review/process.mjs",
                "side": "head",
                "line": 32,
                "checkId": "",
                "quote": "    const abort = () => { cancelled = true; stop(); };\n    signal?.addEventListener('abort', abort, { once: true });"
              },
              {
                "kind": "source",
                "path": "review/process.mjs",
                "side": "head",
                "line": 61,
                "checkId": "",
                "quote": "  if (result.code === 0 && !result.timedOut && !result.cancelled && !result.overflow && !result.spawnError) return result;"
              }
            ]
          }
        ]
